{"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "schema", "document", "Document"], "kwargs": {"metadata": {"Main_Section": "1. The following AI practices shall be prohibited:", "Sub_Section": "**3.4. Interplay between the prohibitions in Article 5(1)(a) and (b) AI Act**", "source": "clean_eu_proh_ai_act.md"}, "page_content": "- (125) In scenarios where both provisions may seem applicable, the primary criterion for differentiation should be the dominant aspect of the exploitation. If the exploitation applies regardless of the specific vulnerabilities of the persons concerned, Article 5(1)(a) AI Act should take precedence, while taking into account the particular effects of the manipulative or deceptive technique on the vulnerable persons\u2019 behaviour and the specific harms that those persons are likely to experience. If the AI-enabled manipulation and exploitation is targeted at a specific vulnerable group of persons due to their age, disability, or specific social or economic situation or aimed to exploit their vulnerabilities, then Article 5(1)(b) AI Act should be applied instead. Exploitation of vulnerabilities of other groups may be covered as part of Article 5(1)(a) AI Act if the purposefully manipulative practice leverage on specific vulnerabilities and weaknesses of those persons.", "type": "Document"}}